+# Attempt account
+
+## Original gauge constraints before estimates
+
+The preceding full scalar gap controlled the physical subspace but used the scalar free Casimir. Inspecting the actual gauge image gave the edge inequality c(j)>=6j_e. Applying that inequality to the same labelled nonlinear source changed its bilinear bound from 8/3 to 2/3, and its original drift bound returned the free physical value three to the full spectrum. The first closed source endpoint and the associated physical primitive are established in G6–31.
+
+## Actual band rather than a trial-state energy
+
+The original first eigenspace contains every plaquette, so the calculation retained the entire matrix rather than one loop quotient. Vacuum, self, disjoint and shared-edge intermediate channels gave B15–16, including each boundary degree. A resolvent contour supplied a uniform all-order remainder. The original L=2 matrix was then enclosed using a full integer power vector and fraction-free inertia, giving B23 for the actual infinite-spin Hamiltonian. Exploratory floating-point eigenvalues were used only before this independent integer certificate; they are not certificate inputs and are not packaged as evidence.
+
+## Dynamical continuation of the source endpoint
+
+An initial improved conditional-influence bound yielded a smaller volume domain than the finite physical estimate. Returning to the original finite semigroup, including its Haar-constant evolution, gave a volume-independent supremum mixing bound. The resulting coupling modulus completed the volume limit at the first endpoint without assigning a finite derivative-row sum there. S24–35 give that full calculation.
+
+## Evaluate the second source before another worst-case estimate
+
+The same local pair channels gave the exact second logarithmic-vacuum coefficient R2. Its original trace norms and the complete anchored-pair count bounded it by 236, instead of the generic 2048/3. That actual coefficient extends the closed source and unique-volume domain to R10–14. R16 retains both physical coefficients in a uniform dynamics comparison. The remaining selected calculation is the actual order-three connected source and its full linearized residual, not a repetition of the now-completed second-source estimate.
